[
 {
  "_comment": "REFLOW PROBE. 20 turns of the v2 cycle on an ILLEGAL primary geometry (portrait primary, 1024x768 not a legal mode -> the engine reflows its UI to a portrait client). QUESTION: does the turn cycle survive a reflowed surface at all? THESIS: it does, because the cycle has exactly ONE pinned aim point -- the inert-chrome ping at (600,6) -- and the top bar spans the client width, so at a ~1080-wide client (600,6) is still bar. FALSIFIED IF: the process dies 0xC0000005, or turn shots are byte-identical (the ping missed, so enter never counted). Requires UIWALK_ALLOW_ILLEGAL_RES=1."
 },
